00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.620
I was like, I can't picture

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.090
anyone else in that role.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.603
- [Meg] It's kind of the
point of the movie, actually.

00:05:15.684 --> 00:05:16.517
- Yeah, you can't picture it, yeah.

00:05:16.517 --> 00:05:17.430
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.871
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:05:18.871 --> 00:05:19.704
- I'll say no more.

00:05:19.704 --> 00:05:20.537
- I'll say no more.

00:05:20.537 --> 00:05:21.390
She's like, I don't wanna spoil it, yeah.

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:22.680
- We shot for 21 days.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.510
We only had a teeny amount of money.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.950
21 nights.
- Yeah.

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.227
- Maybe 18 nights, that was the hard part.

00:05:27.227 --> 00:05:28.710
- The night part.
- Yeah.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:31.410
- That was shot in that
minimal amount of, wow.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:32.400
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.110
And there's just, well,
like we said before,

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:34.943
just two people in it.

00:05:34.943 --> 00:05:36.150
So, I thought it was manageable.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.684
When I got this during the
Covid, I thought, oh, we could,

00:05:39.684 --> 00:05:41.190
(audience laughing)

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.090
we could do this.

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:42.923
We could figure it out.

00:05:42.923 --> 00:05:45.066
There's just two, two, you know.

00:05:45.066 --> 00:05:46.470
It's just very distilled experience.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.360
- And it does play out like a play.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.190
Like, I feel like you
could literally watch this

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.023
on stage on Broadway.

00:05:51.023 --> 00:05:53.036
- Yeah, initially was a play,

00:05:53.036 --> 00:05:55.200
but then it, sort of
basically rewritten, but yeah.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.120
And we shot in Arkansas.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:59.310
We shot in northwest
Arkansas in Bentonville,

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:00.510
which was fantastic.

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:02.038
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Really fantastic with us.

00:06:02.038 --> 00:06:02.871
- Arkansas's beautiful.

00:06:02.871 --> 00:06:03.704
- We loved being there.

00:06:03.704 --> 00:06:05.400
And we shot it in a museum
and the real airport.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:08.176
So we combined it, 'cause it
needed to be a magical world.

00:06:08.176 --> 00:06:09.427
- But in the movie, yeah, in the movie,

00:06:09.427 --> 00:06:10.260
you just think we're in the airport

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.390
and all of a sudden we're
in a beautiful airport

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.940
and not so beautiful airport.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.560
- Well, I love that you
said magical though,

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.480
cause there is a lot of magical realism.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.980
Like, there's things that
happen that I was kinda like,

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.360
when I was watching, I
was like, wait, what?

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.490
I was like, 'cause things
are talking directly at you,

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.260
even in the trailer,
that's kind of given away.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.120
- The environment is a, but you know,

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.571
I always think of it.

00:06:28.571 --> 00:06:30.390
I love the idea that
there's a larger plan.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.190
There's a benevolent force out there

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.763
and it operates on these two idiots,

00:06:34.763 --> 00:06:36.040
(audience laughing)

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:36.873
who can't get it straight.

00:06:36.873 --> 00:06:40.350
And it's a forever sort of
like trying to broker their,

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.870
like, making some peace
or getting some clarity

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.040
or understanding the facts.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.079
Getting some closure, right.

00:06:46.079 --> 00:06:46.912
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:46.912 --> 00:06:49.140
So, I noticed that you
dedicated to Nora Ephron.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.063
So what's your favorite memory of her?

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:54.340
- That's a great question.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.780
She gave great dinner parties,

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:58.890
and they were all,

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.740
and actually, I started
to understand that like,

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:04.920
the being on the set with
her was, the idea was

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.990
that it should feel like
one of her dinner parties.

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:08.610
Like you wanted to talk to everybody,

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:09.660
didn't want it to end.

